<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lewes, Delaware</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lewes is a town in Delaware, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, near Cape Henlopen at the mouth of Delaware Bay. It stands near the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwaanendael">Zwaanendael</a>, the short-lived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> whaling settlement of 1631, and calls itself 'the first town in the first state'. It long served as a base for pilots guiding ships up the bay.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lewes-delaware.jpg" alt="Lewes, Delaware" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harrison Keely · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Second_Street_in_downtown_Lewes,_Delaware.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
